<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <title>Aina Martí – Medical Student</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css" />
</head>
<body>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="logo-block">
      <div class="dna-helix"></div>
      <h1 class="name">AINA MARTÍ</h1>
    </div>
    <nav>
      <a href="#about">About</a>
      <a href="#education">Education</a>
      <a href="#experience">Experience</a>
      <a href="#projects">Projects</a>
      <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </nav>
    <span class="location">Medical student · València, ES</span>
  </header>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-left">
      <p class="hero-tag">MEDICAL STUDENT – VALÈNCIA</p>
      <h2>Aina Martí.</h2>
      <p class="hero-line">Driven by science.<br />Guided by people.</p>
      <button id="enterPortfolio">Enter portfolio</button>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-right">
      <!-- Aquí iría la figura anatómica (imagen) -->
      <div class="body-figure">
        <div class="flow"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <main>
    <section id="about" class="section">
      <h2>Understanding. Then caring.</h2>
      <div class="two-columns">
        <p>
          I want to understand what is happening in the body — and what it means for the person.
        </p>
        <p>
          My interest in Medicine started with questions about how cells and the body work. Today,
          physiology and pathology help me connect those questions to illness and treatment. I’m
          learning to reason through a clinical problem, explain it clearly and make time to listen.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="education" class="section">
      <h2>Education & Training</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Degree in Medicine — Universitat de València</h3>
        <p>Year 1–6. Focus on physiology, pathology, clinical reasoning and patient care.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="experience" class="section">
      <h2>How I learn & work with others</h2>
      <h3>Curiosity. With perspective.</h3>
      <details>
        <summary>Understand the why</summary>
        <p>I connect mechanisms and ideas, then explain the reasoning in my own words. If something does not make sense, I keep asking.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Listen before responding</summary>
        <p>I try to understand the person and the context before giving an answer or suggestion.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Learn my limits</summary>
        <p>I recognise when I need supervision or help and prioritise safety.</p>
      </details>

      <h3>Clinical interests — Questions I want to explore further</h3>
      <div class="three-columns">
        <div>
          <h4>01 Surgery</h4>
          <p>The precision, technical skill and possibility of treating disease through a direct intervention.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4>02 Paediatrics</h4>
          <p>How a child’s body and mind grow and develop, and how care can support that process.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4>03 Oncology</h4>
          <p>The mechanisms of cancer, the questions driving research and the impact of treatment on everyday life.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="note">
        I am particularly interested in childhood cancer care and hope to explore both its medical and surgical perspectives, alongside opportunities to learn about research.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="projects" class="section">
      <h2>Projects</h2>
      <div class="card dark">
        <h3>Let’s go deeper. Salut Nostra Talks. From skin to core.</h3>
        <p>
          Salut Nostra is a personal project to make learning about wellbeing accessible and thought-provoking.
          Season one is in development: 8 perspectives, 8 conversations with health professionals.
        </p>
        <p><strong>What can we learn from those who care?</strong></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="contact" class="section">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>If you’d like to talk about clinical placements, projects or collaborations, you can reach me here.</p>
      <form>
        <label>Name<br /><input type="text" /></label><br />
        <label>Email<br /><input type="email" /></label><br />
        <label>Message<br /><textarea rows="4"></textarea></label><br />
        <button type="submit">Send</button>
      </form>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
